{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "The region of western Roshar around the Purelake, named after an old Silver Kingdom, whose peoples are called Selay.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "52" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "One of the Silver Kingdoms of Roshar, which claimed the Purelake, Marabethia, Babatharnam, Yulay and parts of Tu Bayla and Rira.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-1" }]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "Today some of the Selay are ruled by gerontarchs.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "52" }],
      "fromCulture": "society"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sela Tales held nearly the whole coast of the Purelake.",
      "revealedIn": ["way-of-kings"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The kingdom reached from the Misted Mountains across to the plains of Valhav. The Reshi Sea lay north of it and Makabakam south, with Shin Kak Nish and Iri on its western and northwestern edges, and it also ruled islands out in the Reshi Sea.",
      "revealedIn": ["way-of-kings"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Sela Tales used the Dawnchant for its writing.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-1" },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "4" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-2" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "fromCulture": "language"
    }
